================================================================================
pingap  --  vendored, and the host program of this fork
================================================================================

  Author:     Tree Xie <tree.xie@outlook.com>
  Repository: https://github.com/vicanso/pingap
  Licence:    Apache-2.0
  Version:    0.13.10
  Commit:     51025efca56f342a9a1e5e40559637f32b9140bf  (tag v0.13.10, 2026-08-29)

  The pingap workspace is vendored into this repository. Vendored files keep
  their exact upstream paths so `git merge upstream/main` produces readable
  conflicts inside known files rather than add/delete pairs. Crates owned by this
  fork live under `crates/` instead. The path prefix is the ownership marker:
  unprefixed means vendored and carrying merge debt, `crates/`-prefixed means
  ours and carrying none.

  Vendored at upstream paths: the 19 `pingap-*` crates, `src/` (binary crate),
  `web/` (React admin UI), `conf/`, `benches/`, `docs/`, `examples/`, `website/`,
  `packaging/`, `scripts/`, `hooks/`, `icons/`, `asset/`, `dist/README.md`,
  and the root build and tooling files (`Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `build.rs`,
  `Makefile`, `Dockerfile`, `CLAUDE.md`, `bacon.toml`, `clippy.toml`,
  `typos.toml`, `cliff.toml`, `.rustfmt.toml`, `.cargo/`, `entrypoint.sh`,
  `install.sh`, `publish.sh`, `pingap.service`, `docker-compose.yml`, and the
  README/CHANGELOG/CLA documents).

  Deliberate divergences from the upstream tree, all recorded here because a
  future merge will otherwise read them as accidental drift:

  1. `.github/workflows/publish.yml`, `test.yml`, `pages.yml`, and
     `mark-stale.yaml` are NOT vendored. `publish.yml` triggers on `v*` tags and
     pushes to crates.io and Docker Hub `vicanso/pingap`; `test.yml` (named
     "publish" internally) also carries `IMAGE_NAME: vicanso/pingap`;
     `pages.yml` deploys upstream's site. Vendoring them would mean a release
     tag in this fork attempting a publish under another project's namespace.
     `audit.yml` and `windows.yml` are vendored unchanged.

  2. `.gitignore` retains upstream's content byte-for-byte and appends a
     fork-only section below a marker comment, so the file still merges cleanly.
     `Cargo.lock` is tracked (upstream ignores it as a published library, yet
     force-tracks it anyway) because a reproducible dependency graph is a
     security property for a deployed WAF.

  3. The root `Cargo.toml` gains the five owned crates in `[workspace]` members
     and `[workspace.dependencies]`, an `exclude = ["spikes"]` entry, and a
     `[workspace.lints.clippy]` table. Upstream declares `unwrap_used = "deny"`
     separately in each of its 19 crates and in the root package, with no
     workspace table to inherit from; the new table exists so owned crates opt in
     with `[lints] workspace = true`. No vendored crate manifest was repointed at
     it, since that would be diff with no behaviour change.

  4. `src/plugin/admin.rs` and `src/plugin/mod.rs` are modified to close an admin
     authentication fail-open. Upstream's `auth_validate` returns `true` when the
     resolved credential list is empty, which means an admin listener started
     without credentials serves an unauthenticated config-write API rather than
     denying. See the fork's own history for the change and its tests.

